{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "X1wRGvWRKg", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-02", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761296, "segment_id": "NSxTqz37Ip", "segment_broadcast_id": "X1wRGvWRKg", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Campbell Brown (New York)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 50, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761296, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "X1wRGvWRKg", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-02", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761296, "segment_id": "ct8Vja08qP", "segment_broadcast_id": "X1wRGvWRKg", "segment_title": "September 11 / Commission Report / Political Impact", "segment_description": "(Studio: Campbell Brown) Heightened security following the disclosure of Al Qaeda terror plans, including surveillance of financial targets in New York, New Jersey, & Washington, DC, noted. \n (White House: David Gregory) President Bush\u2019s endorsement of some of the recommendations of the 9/11 Commission, including the creation of a national intelligence director and a national counterterrorism center, featured; details given of opposition from Secretary of Defense Donald Rumsfeld and acting CIA director John McLaughlin&#134;. [BUSH \u2013 says we are a nation in danger; says all the institutions of our government must be prepared for a struggle against terror that will last into the future.] [On the campaign trail, Senator John KERRY \u2013 criticizes Bush for not having a sense of urgency; asserts terrorists are using our actions as a means of recruitment.]", "segment_duration": 180, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63050.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761297, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "X1wRGvWRKg", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-02", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761296, "segment_id": "1fJF1TBqMu", "segment_broadcast_id": "X1wRGvWRKg", "segment_title": "Defending America: How Safe? How Soon? (Part I)", "segment_description": "(Studio: Campbell Brown) Special series about the recommendations of the 9/11 Commission introduced. \n (Washington: Andrea Mitchell) A look at whether the creation of a national intelligence director and a national counterterrorism center will make America safer and how long it will take presented; details given of concern about transferring responsibility for paramilitary operations to the Defense Department. [Former Secretary of Defense William COHEN\u2020- comments on removing impediments that have prevented more rapid action in the past.] [Former CIA covert operative Jack DEVINE\u2020- warns about the logistical obstacles of setting up a new office.] [Government efficiency expert Paul LIGHT\u2020- says we often add a new layer of bureaucracy.] [White House chief of staff Andrew CARD\u2020- says the president has put forth the right solution to meet the terrorist threat.] [Former CIA director Robert GATES\u2020- comments on the difficulty in making changes in the midst of a political campaign.]", "segment_duration": 180, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63230.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761298, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "X1wRGvWRKg", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-02", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761296, "segment_id": "gUYs56eaPz", "segment_broadcast_id": "X1wRGvWRKg", "segment_title": "Terrorism / Al Qaeda Threat / Financial Institutions", "segment_description": "(Studio: Campbell Brown) Report introduced.   (Washington: Pete Williams) The information that led to the terror threat targeting financial institutions {listed} in the New York City area and Washington, DC, featured; details given of information obtained from the computer of an Al Qaeda operative captured in Pakistan. [Secretary of Homeland Security Tom RIDGE \u2013 affirms the reliability of the sources.] [Terrorism expert Sara DALY&#134;- says the terrorists will continue this jihad until it is finished.]   (Studio: Campbell Brown) Report introduced.   (New York: Tom Costello) The reaction of workers at the targeted sites to the terror threat featured; scenes shown of security measures & Senator Charles Schumer greeting workers at the New York Stock Exchange. [New York Stock Exchange CEO John THAIN&#134;- says we intend to keep the exchange functioning.] [2 New York City RESIDENTS \u2013 comment.] [Washington, DC, police department Chief Charles RAMSEY&#134;- says we have to be vigilant & aware of any possibility.]   (Studio: Campbell Brown) First Lady Laura Bush shown having coffee with New York\u2019s governor & mayor in the lobby of Citigroup\u2019s headquarters.", "segment_duration": 280, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63410.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761299, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "X1wRGvWRKg", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-02", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761296, "segment_id": "NlNc6lwKW1", "segment_broadcast_id": "X1wRGvWRKg", "segment_title": "Stock Market Report (Studio: Campbell Brown)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 10, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63690.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761300, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "X1wRGvWRKg", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-02", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761296, "segment_id": "eA0xEPwpiV", "segment_broadcast_id": "X1wRGvWRKg", "segment_title": "Upcoming Items (Studio: Campbell Brown)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 10, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63700.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761301, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "X1wRGvWRKg", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-02", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "le